  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Tuesday)\n\nWeak instability across northeastern Nevada overnight will \ncontinue to produce isolated (5-15% chance) thunderstorm activity \nthrough the early to mid-morning hours. Storms are expected to \nproduce very little rainfall, generally less than a tenth of an \ninch. Mostly sunny across the entire CWA late this morning and \nafternoon with dry and storm free conditions along with relatively\nlight winds to around 10 mph. \n\nThe area will be under a short-lived post frontal regime later \ntoday before ridging builds back into the southwestern CONUS for \nmuch of the rest of this week. This will allow warm afternoon high\ntemperatures to continue through Thursday ranging 10 to 15 \ndegrees above normal in the low to mid 80s. \n\nBeyond Friday the ridging over the region gets squeezed eastward \nas a large longwave ULT pushes into the Pacific Northwest Friday \nevening. This will tighten the gradient over the area bringing the\npotential for gusty winds and impactful precipitation by the \nweekend.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Moderate confidence exists in \ncontinued warm temperatures each afternoon through this week. Very\nlow confidence exists in the potential for an impactful storm \nsystem through the area this weekend.",
